<title>USA: IOWA-SO MINN HOGS ESTIMATE FRIDAY 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>IOWA-SO MINN HOGS ESTIMATE FRIDAY 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts:</p>
<p>Friday - 100,000   Wk ago: 82,000  Yr ago: 100,000</p>
<p>Saturday- 20,000   Wk ago: 10,000  Yr ago:   9,000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were steady, instances $0.50 per cwt higher than midsession Thursday. Trade and demand light to moderate. Offerings moderate.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    54.50 -56.00	   55.50 -57.00</p>
<p>few			53.50 -54.00		   -57.50</p>
<p>few							    56.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    53.50 -56.00	   54.00 -57.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    53.50 -56.00	   54.00 -57.00</p>
<p>Sows:  steady.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-500 lbs   42.00 -45.00	   43.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    46.00 -49.50	   47.00 -50.50</p>
<p>Compared last week:  barrows and gilts .50 higher.  Slaughter sows under 500 lbs steady; over 500 lbs steady to 1.50 higher.</p>
<p>Receipts this week estimated at 534,000 compared 492,000 last week and 492,000 a year ago. Barrow and gilt average weight for week ending 2 Aug 1997 was 248.9, compared with 250.0 previous week and 244.2 a year ago.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
